# THE PACKS THAT ARRIVED EMPTY. Drop them here and stop thinking about formats.
#
# This folder exists because of a real failure. On 22 Aug all 28 Quaternius
# character packs were copied in; 20 folders reached git and only 10 of those
# carried a model. The other 10 arrived as a stray Preview.png and 8 never
# appeared at all — because ../characters/.gitignore keeps glTF and drops
# everything else, and git cannot store a folder with no surviving files. No
# error, no warning, nine days before anyone noticed.
#
# So the rule here is the opposite one: keep EVERY format the ingest can read,
# and let the ingest decide which to use. Uploading a duplicate wastes some
# history; losing a pack silently wastes weeks.
#
#   tools/ingest-characters.mjs prefers .glb, then .gltf, then .fbx, and skips
#   an FBX whose glTF it has already packed — so a pack that ships both is
#   ingested losslessly and the FBX is ignored rather than overwriting it.
#
# Run `node tools/check-incoming.mjs` after any upload. It prints, per pack,
# what git actually kept and names any folder that will vanish.

# ignore everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories
!*/

# ...and keep every model format, because guessing wrong loses the pack
!*.glb
!*.gltf
!*.bin
!*.fbx

# textures a .gltf references by filename, and the FBX sibling textures
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg

!LICENSE*
!License*
!license*
!README.md
!.gitignore
